@startuml
' newpage splits the diagram so each page fits landscape A4: PlantUML exports
' seq-internal-parcel-api.png, seq-internal-parcel-api_001.png, ... (one file per page).
title Sequence Diagram - Internal Parcel API (1 of 4)
caption SwiftDrop parcel-service (Role 3)

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam dpi 200
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 110
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor black
  LifeLineBorderColor #555555
  ParticipantBorderColor black
  ParticipantBackgroundColor white
  BoxBorderColor black
  BoxBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  GroupBorderColor black
  GroupBackgroundColor #E8E8E8
  DividerBorderColor black
  DividerBackgroundColor #E8E8E8
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor black
  BackgroundColor white
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor black
  BackgroundColor white
}

participant "merchant-service\n:8085" as MS
participant "notification-service\n:8086" as NS
box "parcel-service :8083" #F2F2F2
  participant "Internal-token\nfilter (common)" as SEC
  participant "InternalParcel\nController" as ICTRL
  participant "ParcelService" as SVC
  participant "PricingService\nClient" as PC
end box
participant "pricing-service\n:8082" as PR
database "parcel_db" as DB

== 1. Merchant order creates a parcel ==
note over MS
  merchant-service has already checked
  the X-API-Key and that the merchant
  is APPROVED (seq-merchant-order, Role 5).
end note
MS -> SEC : POST /internal/parcels\nX-Internal-Token\n(InternalRestClientFactory)\n{merchantId, pickupAddress,\npickupZone, dropoffAddress,\ndropoffZone, recipientName,\nrecipientPhone, recipientEmail,\nsize, weightKg, speed}
SEC -> SEC : compare with\nINTERNAL_API_TOKEN\n(constant time)
alt missing or wrong token
  SEC --> MS : 401 ProblemDetail
end
SEC -> ICTRL : forward\n(ROLE_INTERNAL_SERVICE)
ICTRL -> ICTRL : @Valid request\n(no fee field is accepted)
alt invalid or missing fields
  ICTRL --> MS : 400 ProblemDetail\nwith field errors
end
ICTRL -> SVC : createMerchantParcel(\nrequest)
newpage Sequence Diagram - Internal Parcel API (2 of 4)
== 1. Merchant order creates a parcel (continued) ==
SVC -> PC : getQuote(pickupZone,\ndropoffZone, weightKg,\nsize, speed)
PC -> PR : POST /internal/pricing/quote\n(X-Internal-Token)
alt valid quote
  PR --> PC : 200 {routeType, baseFee,\nweightFee, sizeFee, expressFee,\ndiscount, total, currency}
  PC --> SVC : quote
else weight does not fit the size
  PR --> PC : 400 ProblemDetail
  PC --> MS : 400 validation error\n(via SVC, ICTRL), nothing saved
else pricing down, slow or unreachable
  PR --> PC : 5xx / timeout
  PC --> MS : 503 Service Unavailable\n(via SVC, ICTRL), nothing saved
end

newpage Sequence Diagram - Internal Parcel API (3 of 4)
== 1. Merchant order creates a parcel (continued) ==
SVC -> DB : generate tracking number\nSD-XXXX-XXXX and check\nit is not already used
group One transaction (@Transactional)
  SVC -> DB : INSERT parcels\n(merchant_id, customer_id = null,\nzones, recipient_email,\nfee breakdown, status CREATED)
  SVC -> DB : INSERT parcel_status_history\n(CREATED, changed_by = merchantId,\nrole MERCHANT,\nnote "Merchant order created")
  SVC -> DB : INSERT outbox_events\n(ParcelStatusChanged v1 with\nmerchantId, routing key\nparcel.status.created)
  SVC -> DB : COMMIT
end
SVC --> MS : 201 Created\nLocation: /internal/parcels/{id}\n{id, trackingNo, status: CREATED,\nfeeAmount, feeCurrency}\n(via ICTRL)
note over SVC, DB
  The fee always comes from the pricing quote; a fee sent by
  a merchant is never used (architecture section 8). The outbox
  relay then publishes parcel.status.created, and webhook.q leads
  notification-service to send the signed webhook to the merchant.
end note

newpage Sequence Diagram - Internal Parcel API (4 of 4)
== 2. notification-service looks up the recipient ==
note over NS
  Runs for each ParcelStatusChanged
  event. Events carry IDs only, so the
  contact details are fetched here.
end note
NS -> SEC : GET /internal/parcels/\n{parcelId}/contacts\nX-Internal-Token
SEC -> SEC : compare with\nINTERNAL_API_TOKEN
alt missing or wrong token
  SEC --> NS : 401 ProblemDetail
end
SEC -> ICTRL : forward\n(ROLE_INTERNAL_SERVICE)
ICTRL -> SVC : getContacts(parcelId)
SVC -> DB : SELECT recipient_name,\nrecipient_phone, recipient_email\nWHERE id = parcelId
alt unknown parcel
  SVC --> NS : 404 Not Found (via ICTRL)
end
SVC --> NS : 200 {recipientName,\nrecipientPhone, recipientEmail}\n(via ICTRL)
note over NS
  Who is notified (architecture 6.3):
  customer booking: email to the customer
  (from auth-service), SMS to the recipient;
  merchant order: email and SMS to the
  recipient. SMS only on OUT_FOR_DELIVERY,
  DELIVERED and FAILED.
end note
note over SEC, DB
  The reply is personal data: private network only, internal token
  required, never logged (masked) and never put into events.
  recipientEmail is null for customer bookings.
  Status changes from dispatch-service use PATCH
  /internal/parcels/{id}/status: see activity-parcel-status-update.
end note

@enduml
